id: pm-lint-lint-baselines
title: Acknowledge lint debt with source-bound evidence
description: Add typed finding acknowledgments and a complete baseline gate that preserves old debt and fails new regressions.
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T20:08:40.639Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T20:19:00.176Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Changed text invalidates acknowledgment; Broad rule disabling cannot hide new findings; Output distinguishes debt from new failures; Typed SDK and CLI with compact TOON/JSON, refusals and remedies; README example and measured public tracker validation without git; CI npm and Bun release gates pass at unchanged thresholds"
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T20:08:47.021Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked: src/rules.ts already ships ten authoring rules. The pinned core SDK governance assurance surface stores policy and measurements; pm-ops assurance.ts and README describe package readiness. Neither provides source-bound item-authoring finding acknowledgments. This feature stays in pm-lint. Reconciliation PR #17 closes pm-lint-epic, which remains untouched. Design: specific item/rule/version/full-source digest plus reason, strict baseline validation, complete default-policy scans, visible debt and new counts, no git dependency."
  "2026-10-21T20:13:10.989Z",codex-agent,"Implemented strict portable acknowledgments, full canonical source hashes, visible debt/new/stale counts, complete default-policy baseline checks and exclusive atomic baseline writes. Targeted baseline, command and engine tests: 23 passed, including a non-git tracker subprocess with no git executable. Typecheck and lint passed. Baseline mode gates new findings at every severity; ordinary lint retains its existing threshold behavior."
  "2026-10-21T20:17:08.204Z",codex-agent,"Public validation: committed public pm-ops tracker at eba7d5262fd75e67afce0caad29dae7dc7dfbaeb, read-only non-git snapshot, 146 certified/scanned items, 24 findings (10 PML002 errors, 10 PML005 warnings, 4 PML006 info). Exact acknowledgments retained 24 debt, 0 new/stale, exit 0. Separate mutation copy: 23 debt, 1 new, 1 stale, exit 1; broad disabling refused. Snapshot byte inventory unchanged. Behavioral revert proof: replacing sourceDigest, isAcknowledged and assertBaselinePolicy with non-enforcing behavior made all 3 selected regressions fail; restored immediately. Command: node --test --test-name-pattern \"source digest|baseline retains|baseline refuses\" test/baseline.test.ts. No SDK mocks; disk-write fault injection tests atomic preservation."
  "2026-10-21T20:18:46.541Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted baseline coverage: 8 tests passed; baseline.ts and baseline-file.ts measured 100% statements, branches, functions and lines. Linked targeted suite passed 23/23 through pm test --run --progress (project test-result tracking is disabled, so the receipt is documented here). Fixed lock cleanup so a successful publisher cannot remove a subsequent writer lock. Source typecheck, lint, zero-duplication and docstring gates are being finalized; full npm/Bun gates are delegated to CI as requested. Local strict health reports merge_fence_drift after restoring the preexisting tracked fence changed by dependency prepare; no merge-driver work or history repair performed. CI uses its normal npm ci preparation."
